Author: Christoph Kieslich <c.kieslich@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 17 20:34:22 2026 +0000

    Submission: bind the Main Worker's Organization namespace, not a private copy (#231)

    SubmissionWorker did `yield* Organization`, which hosts a second Organization
    namespace on the Submission Worker. Its setup reads INVITATION_TOKEN_KEY, which that
    Worker does not have, so every call into it died and POST /exchange answered 500
    (with no CORS headers, so the browser reported a CORS error). The adapter test
    reproduced it on local workerd: RpcCallError on getTestSubmissionContext and on
    previewTestAnswers.

    Organization is now a lightweight class with its implementation in `OrganizationLive`,
    which only the Main Worker provides; the Submission Worker binds the Main Worker's
    namespace with `Organization.from`. Organization.test.ts deploys both Workers and
    exchanges a real test Invitation's token. A crash behind submissionRoutes now answers
    a plain JSON 500 that keeps the CORS headers.

    Moving the class off a Worker that hosts it needs two deploys, so the Submission
    Worker's private binding is dropped by the change before this one.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

